186094918 #edb/ref 1080 "-e^{x} + \\frac{1}{x}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094918 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094918 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d160ad97-ce05-5c09-a415-37e669bc37d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094919 #edb/ref 1080 "-5e^{x} - \\ln 3 + \\frac{2}{x}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094919 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094919 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f0f5dc19-0891-5c65-ba47-3963e6e0a451" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094920 #edb/ref 1080 "-5e^{x} + \\frac{2}{x}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094920 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094920 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fdb7af8c-26aa-56d2-9b2c-2028d177a3e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096413 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3627" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096413 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $y=5\\ln x$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096413 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6624681a-bb00-59db-8df9-4d5a3cd00434" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096413 #edb/ref 1074 "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{ \\textrm{d} x}\\left( \\ln x \\right)= \\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}   & = \\left(5\\ln x\\right)'\\  \n                                                    & = 5 (\\ln x)'\\\n                                                    &=5\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{x}\\\n                                                    &= \\dfrac{5}{x}.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t  \n\n}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096414 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3628" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096414 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)=2\\ln x+x^2-1$, find $f'(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096414 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "58d47fb0-cf75-58c4-8eea-f3ae97333159" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096414 #edb/ref 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\tf'(x) &= \\left(2\\ln x+x^2-1\\right)'\\\n\t\t\t&=2 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{x}+2x-0\\\n\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{2}{x}+2x.\n\n}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096415 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3629" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096415 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $y=4\\log_3 x,$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096415 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f61ac550-d62c-558f-b6d5-0d4c9aba8089" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096415 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we apply our formula for the derivative when the base of the logarithm is a number other than $e.$ By doing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}&=\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(4\\log_3 x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t &=4\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\log_3 x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t &=4\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{x \\ln 3}\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{4}{x \\ln 3}.\n\n}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096416 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3630" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096416 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $y= \\log_4 x + \\ln x$,  find the slope of the tangent at $x=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096416 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5eaa00f8-0fd0-5de6-a7c0-965db6de3a5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096416 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left( \\log_4 x + \\ln x \\right)\\\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\log_4 x) + \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\ln x )\\\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 4} + \\dfrac{1}{x}.\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{1}{xln⁡4}+\\frac{1}{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{ln⁡4}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096613 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048932 #edb/ref 1