 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096894 #edb/ref 1045 "Differentiating Logarithmic Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096894 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186097419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096894 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096894 #edb/ref 1050 660.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186096894 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "a08f28ad-f5a0-5009-8802-2bc2d37a5e98" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097156 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097156 #edb/ref 1069 "q-1919" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097156 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097156 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={11}^{x}-5ln⁡x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097156 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1cb4423b-343c-5035-85a6-f38acaa8835d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097156 #edb/ref 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({11}^{x}-5ln⁡x) \\\\  & ={11}^{x}\\cdot ln⁡11-5(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & ={11}^{x}ln⁡11-\\frac{5}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097157 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186094915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097157 #edb/ref 1069 "q-1920" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097157 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ for $y =-5e^{x} + 2\\ln x$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097157 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e09c4141-d749-574e-b1a3-1f49f5b7e3d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097419 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097419 #edb/ref 1061 12313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097419 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c57de084-771c-5781-b9e0-8c1803097cbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097419 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097420 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097420 #edb/ref 1061 12314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097420 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b0bc4f64-4ed3-59b3-8f89-94255173749b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097420 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097421 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097421 #edb/ref 1061 12315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097421 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f8894432-f206-54fd-8d25-0650b8854e56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097421 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097422 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097422 #edb/ref 1061 12316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097422 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "50c40528-51c7-55e5-8f01-7af56b1066fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097422 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097423 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097423 #edb/ref 1061 12317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097423 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "386f854e-f0f4-5871-a66f-7812d943cd5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097423 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097424 #edb/ref 1061 12319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097424 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "346741f6-8687-5172-973e-c1b1ec2d6336" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097424 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097816 #edb/ref 1064 "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{ \\textrm{d} x}\\left( \\ln x \\right)= \\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe'll prove this result in a future lesson." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097816 #edb/ref 1065 2615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097816 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b1f46211-3766-53d0-bcc7-30bb9056b948" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097816 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097817 #edb/ref 1064 "For a general logarithm of base $a,$ the derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{ \\textrm{d} x}\\left( \\log_a x \\right)= \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln a}.\n$$\n\nAlso, recall that whenever $\\log$ is written without a base, we can assume that it represents the base $10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\log x =  \\log_{10} x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(\\operatorname{log}x) & =\\frac{d}{dx}({log}_{10}x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** To see where this rule comes from, we can use the change-of-base formula as shown below.\n\n$$\n\\log_a x = \\dfrac{\\ln x}{\\ln a}\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative and using the fact that $\\ln a$ is a constant, then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}x}{\\operatorname{ln}a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}a}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}a}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097817 #edb/ref 1065 2616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097817 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7a7450e4-ec0e-5a5e-9c86-9430eb889be7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097817 #edb/ref 1067 "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function with a General Base" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284929 #edb/ref 1080 "{11}^{x}-ln⁡11-\\frac{5}{x}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284929 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284929 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1045aaaf-0a76-5469-afdc-876ec049ae29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286338 #edb/ref 1080 "{11}^{x}ln⁡x-\\frac{1}{x}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286338 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286338 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aa30aba2-91df-575b-9e42-a1c8a2d47cbf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286556 #edb/ref 1080 "ln⁡11+\\frac{5}{x}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286556 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286556 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c13aff45-c853-5d8b-ae11-7b4d6b