077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314045 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186312275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314045 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0bb11537-ff22-5776-85db-c4e4d92da407" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314550 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186312439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314550 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314550 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314550 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186312439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314550 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c1560d5a-5716-563a-970a-84ea931d3b0b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314898 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314898 #edb/ref 1069 "q-339994" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314898 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314898 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the function $y=2{x}^{3}+x-3{log}_{6}⁡x,$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=3$ is\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314898 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b9fb0b98-97be-5fa4-a0a8-73b036fd9d03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314898 #edb/ref 1074 "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}+x-3{log}_{6}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+1-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡6} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{xln⁡6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(6{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{xln⁡6})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =6(3)^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{3\\cdot ln⁡6} \\\\  & =55-\\frac{1}{ln⁡6}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314912 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314912 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340104" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314912 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314912 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the function  $y=4ln⁡x-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}+5$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=2$ is\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314912 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "905686ba-b3f6-58e7-998d-63ec7c2c2866" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314912 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4ln⁡x-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}+5) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}ln⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(\\frac{4}{x}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}ln⁡(2))|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{2}ln⁡(2) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{4}{3}ln⁡(2)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428108 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428108 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: en